  "title": "Reconfigurable Virtual Memory for FPGA-Driven I/O",
  "abstract": "FPGAs are increasingly used to accelerate modern applications, and cloud providers offer FPGA platforms on-demand with a variety of FPGAs, I/O peripherals, and memory options. FPGA vendors expose I/O with low-level interfaces that limit application portability. Current approaches to abstracting these interfaces trade level of abstraction against performance.",
